# NOTE: .claude/ is intentionally tracked as a working example
# Users can copy this to their own projects
# See examples/ for clean templates

# Internal scripts (not for distribution). NOTE: 'scripts/*' not
# 'scripts/' -- git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY
# is excluded, so the negation below only works against a glob.
scripts/*
# ...except the repair tool users are told to run. server.py and models.py
# both name this path in error messages shown to the operator, and
# tests/test_tool_call_envelope.py loads it, so excluding it published an
# instruction pointing at a file nobody who clones the repo has.
!scripts/clean_tool_call_envelopes.py

# CLAUDE.md is NOT ignored. This repository ships its own, tests/test_claims.py
# reads it (C07 checks its hook table against the shipped templates), and the
# docs-sync rule requires updating it with every behaviour change. The rule
# that used to sit here said users create their own, which was true of other
# projects and never of this one, and `git ls-files --ignored -c` listed the
# contradiction.

# LoCoMo evaluation data: CC BY-NC 4.0, fetched by the operator, never vendored.
# docs/locomo-results/*.json are OUR aggregate measurements and ARE committed.
locomo10.json
msc_personas_all.json

# Row-level research output. The per-run totals in docs/locomo-results and
# docs/bridge-results ARE committed, because the claim ledger checks the
# numbers in the write-ups against them. These two patterns are the bulk:
# 1.6 MB of per-question outcomes and 112 KB of per-query note identifiers,
# which nothing reads and which carry one operator's store contents.
# Regenerate with `python -m tests.locomo_benchmark` and
# `python -m tests.bridge_benchmark --sweep`.
docs/locomo-results/pq-*.json
docs/bridge-results/bridge-on.json
docs/bridge-results/bridge-off.json
docs/bridge-results/bridge-min*.json
